From: sunshineinabox <aqemail@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 04:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] iommu/arm-smmu-qcom: Add SM8750 MDSS compatible

Add the SM8750 MDSS compatible to the clients list, so it gets an
identity domain at boot, as SM8550 and SM8650 do since the two previous
patches.

The bootloader leaves its picture scanning out at kernel entry. Without
an identity domain the MDSS stream is attached to an empty translating
domain as soon as the device is added, and its fetches fault until the
DPU driver stops the timing engine and attaches its own domain. On the
KONKR Pocket FIT Elite every boot logged, right after "Adding to iommu
group" and with the group's type DMA-FQ, as many of these as the rate
limit lets through:

  arm-smmu 15000000.iommu: Unhandled context fault: fsr=0x402,
  iova=0xfc800100, fsynr=0x7d0021, cbfrsynra=0x800, cb=7
---
 drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/arm-smmu-qcom.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/arm-smmu-qcom.c b/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/arm-smmu-qcom.c
--- a/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/arm-smmu-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/arm-smmu-qcom.c
@@ -428,6 +428,7 @@ static const struct of_device_id qcom_smmu_client_of_match[] __maybe_unused = {
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm8450-mdss" },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm8550-mdss" },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm8650-mdss" },
+	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm8750-mdss" },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,x1e80100-mdss" },
 	{ }
 };
